WEBVTT

00:01:33.500 --> 00:01:34.620
Today, the city will have moderate rain.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.739
The temperature will be 26 to 31 degrees.

00:01:36.739 --> 00:01:37.939
For the next three days,

00:01:38.099 --> 00:01:39.659
there will be thunderstorms or heavy rain.

00:01:40.060 --> 00:01:41.379
Be sure to take an umbrella when you go out.

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.700
Dad, I'll be waiting for you in Shenzhen tomorrow.

00:02:26.139 --> 00:02:26.620
Dad.

00:02:28.020 --> 00:02:29.219
You must be tired. Let me.

00:02:29.219 --> 00:02:30.659
Didn't I tell you not to come pick me up?

00:02:30.659 --> 00:02:32.219
Did it make Xiaoxiao late for her piano lesson?

00:02:32.219 --> 00:02:32.860
No, it didn't.

00:02:32.860 --> 00:02:34.300
We can go pick her up right now.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:34.740
I'll get it.

00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:35.860
Let me, let me. Where's the car?

00:02:36.020 --> 00:02:36.580
Over here.

00:02:50.500 --> 00:02:51.740
The last time you were in Shenzhen

00:02:51.819 --> 00:02:53.300
was the year Xiaoxiao was born.

00:02:54.219 --> 00:02:54.740
Look.

00:02:54.939 --> 00:02:55.939
See how much it's changed?

00:02:56.340 --> 00:02:56.819
A lot.

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:13.900
It's been over forty years,

00:03:14.219 --> 00:03:15.180
and it's still a landmark.

00:03:29.460 --> 00:03:30.699
Keep your fingers arched.

00:03:30.900 --> 00:03:31.939
Don't let them collapse.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:33.860
Here.

00:03:40.460 --> 00:03:41.139
Right here.

00:03:45.379 --> 00:03:46.340
Very good.

00:03:47.979 --> 00:03:48.860
Hold it.

00:03:49.259 --> 00:03:50.620
Look at how she plays the piano.

00:03:51.139 --> 00:03:52.099
Isn't she adorable?

00:03:53.659 --> 00:03:55.659
You never doted on me like that.

00:04:16.500 --> 00:04:17.660
What piece is she playing?

00:04:18.459 --> 00:04:19.180
I don't know.

00:05:00.500 --> 00:05:01.379
Where are you off to, Brother Lu?

00:05:01.459 --> 00:05:02.420
Looking for your wife again?

00:05:03.060 --> 00:05:04.500
What, are you jealous?

00:05:05.019 --> 00:05:06.100
Like you're the only one with a partner.

00:05:07.779 --> 00:05:08.620
Let me tell you,

00:05:08.620 --> 00:05:09.300
my wife

00:05:09.620 --> 00:05:10.660
is the best in the world.

00:05:12.899 --> 00:05:13.459
Mingshu.

00:05:29.459 --> 00:05:30.420
There, it's done.

00:05:31.899 --> 00:05:33.100
You made this?

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:35.300
It actually looks pretty good.

00:05:35.699 --> 00:05:36.819
I copied it from a magazine.

00:05:37.259 --> 00:05:38.420
It gets the idea across, right?

00:05:38.420 --> 00:05:39.180
Just a rough version.

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.139
You can use this to practice your fingering for now.

00:05:41.459 --> 00:05:43.220
Someday, we'll be able to buy a real one.

00:05:43.899 --> 00:05:45.379
You've really changed since coming to Shenzhen.

00:05:45.540 --> 00:05:46.779
Daring to dream of anything.

00:05:46.779 --> 00:05:47.939
Why wouldn't I dare to dream?

00:05:48.180 --> 00:05:48.740
Back in the day,

00:05:48.740 --> 00:05:49.939
when we were building five-story buildings,

00:05:50.060 --> 00:05:51.139
who would have thought that one day

00:05:51.139 --> 00:05:51.579
we could

00:05:51.579 --> 00:05:52.740
build a fifty-story skyscraper?

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:56.100
As long as you dare to dream and work hard,

00:05:56.699 --> 00:05:57.699
life will always get better.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:05:59.139
Alright.

00:05:59.139 --> 00:06:00.420
Don't be in such a hurry to eat.

00:06:00.420 --> 00:06:01.579
Try it first.

00:06:01.939 --> 00:06:02.500
Try it.

00:06:05.180 --> 00:06:06.660
These hands are used to tying rebar.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:07.980
That's why they're so strong.

00:06:08.699 --> 00:06:09.819
Others might play for ten minutes,

00:06:10.139 --> 00:06:11.060
but you could play all night.

00:06:13.379 --> 00:06:14.339
Okay, I'll try.

00:06:30.980 --> 00:06:31.939
It's actually pretty good.

00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:11.060
Dad.

00:07:12.060 --> 00:07:13.500
Mom's been gone for so many years now.

00:07:13.579 --> 00:07:15.060
You've been alone all this time.

00:07:16.139 --> 00:07:17.500
If someday

00:07:17.579 --> 00:07:19.379
you want to find a new companion,

00:07:19.699 --> 00:07:21.259
don't worry about my opinion.

00:07:21.379 --> 00:07:22.500
I'll definitely support you.

00:07:25.180 --> 00:07:26.740
I won't pressure you to have a second child,

00:07:27.699 --> 00:07:29.060
so don't you pressure me to remarry.

00:07:30.740 --> 00:07:32.379
Look who's being rebellious now.

00:07:33.060 --> 00:07:34.139
People of our generation,

00:07:35.459 --> 00:07:36.899
we focus on doing one thing well in life,

00:07:37.459 --> 00:07:38.500
and staying with one person.

00:07:39.019 --> 00:07:39.620
That's enough.

00:07:43.459 --> 00:07:45.180
Whether your mom is here or not,

00:07:46.379 --> 00:07:47.699
my heart is still full.

00:07:51.379 --> 00:07:51.939
Here.

00:08:01.740 --> 00:08:02.579
I heard

00:08:02.899 --> 00:08:03.860
this time, over thirty couples

00:08:03.860 --> 00:08:05.060
came to work as husband-and-wife teams.

00:08:05.459 --> 00:08:06.500
To speed things up,

00:08:06.500 --> 00:08:07.620
they're not even allowed to live together.

00:08:12.019 --> 00:08:12.699
Don't forget,

00:08:13.139 --> 00:08:15.180
you promised to marry me the day the building is finished.

00:08:18.139 --> 00:08:19.500
Who promised you that?

00:08:21.259 --> 00:08:22.259
The night before we left Jingmen,

00:08:22.259 --> 00:08:23.060
you said it yourself.

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:24.459
Don't even think about backing out.

00:08:30.259 --> 00:08:31.939
It seems the higher-ups' intention this time

00:08:31.939 --> 00:08:33.460
is dead set on using slipforming.

00:08:34.379 --> 00:08:35.820
We've tried it twice and failed both times.

00:08:36.220 --> 00:08:37.580
Who knows when we'll ever

00:08:37.700 --> 00:08:39.179
see this building topped out.

00:08:42.259 --> 00:08:43.500
Listen to me, fellow property owners.

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:44.539
Perhaps you all

00:08:44.539 --> 00:08:46.700
aren't too familiar

00:08:46.820 --> 00:08:47.580
with this traditional jump form technique.

00:08:47.940 --> 00:08:49.259
Let me demonstrate for you.

00:08:49.500 --> 00:08:50.379
This is the foundation.

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:53.700
Jump forming first requires pouring the first layer.

00:08:54.820 --> 00:08:55.820
After pouring it in,

00:08:55.940 --> 00:08:57.580
you have to wait at least two days

00:08:57.580 --> 00:08:59.259
for the concrete to set.

00:09:00.379 --> 00:09:01.500
Then you dismantle this formwork,

00:09:01.700 --> 00:09:04.259
and then build the second layer of formwork.

00:09:04.940 --> 00:09:06.700
Then pour concrete in again,

00:09:06.700 --> 00:09:08.820
and have to wait another two-plus days

00:09:09.179 --> 00:09:11.820
for the concrete to set before dismantling.

00:09:11.820 --> 00:09:14.340
Then the third layer pour,

00:09:14.580 --> 00:09:17.019
and so on, layer by layer going up.

00:09:17.019 --> 00:09:19.259
Our project is over fifty stories high.

00:09:19.740 --> 00:09:20.820
Getting anxious is useless.

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:21.580
But if we switch to

00:09:21.580 --> 00:09:23.059
our slipforming technique,

00:09:23.539 --> 00:09:25.100
that's a whole different story.

00:09:25.700 --> 00:09:26.820
Slipforming works like this.

00:09:27.340 --> 00:09:28.539
This is the pour body.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:30.340
This is the pouring.

00:09:30.659 --> 00:09:31.980
We pour the concrete

00:09:32.059 --> 00:09:33.580
directly in like this,

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:38.220
while simultaneously lifting it upward.

00:09:39.980 --> 00:09:41.299
After pouring in the concrete,

00:09:41.779 --> 00:09:43.700
we only need to pause briefly for two hours.

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:44.860
Once the concrete sets,

00:09:45.980 --> 00:09:47.100
we inject more concrete,

00:09:48.220 --> 00:09:51.059
lift and pour again after two hours,

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:51.980
and keep lifting.

00:09:52.580 --> 00:09:54.220
Once it sets, we continue.

00:09:54.820 --> 00:09:55.700
Like this.

00:09:58.659 --> 00:09:59.980
Its efficiency and quality,

00:09:59.980 --> 00:10:02.340
especially the smoothness

00:10:02.340 --> 00:10:03.820
of the building's exterior,

00:10:03.980 --> 00:10:06.059
are something traditional methods

00:10:06.059 --> 00:10:07.340
can never achieve.

00:10:08.179 --> 00:10:09.220
You can all calculate it.

00:10:09.220 --> 00:10:10.779
Which method is more scientific

00:10:10.820 --> 00:10:12.179
and more suitable

00:10:12.179 --> 00:10:13.580
in terms of time and efficiency?

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:15.940
Alright.

00:10:17.460 --> 00:10:18.700
Thank you, Master Fu, for the explanation.

00:10:19.179 --> 00:10:21.299
I wonder if after listening,

00:10:21.299 --> 00:10:22.179
you property owners

00:10:22.179 --> 00:10:23.299
are now able

00:10:23.580 --> 00:10:24.659
to understand more clearly

00:10:24.659 --> 00:10:26.580
why we insist on slipforming.

00:10:28.580 --> 00:10:29.539
We understand, alright.

00:10:29.940 --> 00:10:31.580
It sounds impressive.

00:10:31.740 --> 00:10:34.340
But so far in this country,

00:10:34.340 --> 00:10:35.860
there hasn't been a single successful precedent.

00:10:36.659 --> 00:10:38.460
You've already failed twice.

00:10:38.700 --> 00:10:40.179
How much manpower and resources,

00:10:40.179 --> 00:10:40.860
and financial resources were wasted?

00:10:41.179 --> 00:10:42.340
Will you keep going?

00:10:42.899 --> 00:10:44.019
Failing twice

00:10:44.019 --> 00:10:45.460
means we've gained experience twice.

00:10:45.940 --> 00:10:47.460
But who's responsible for the delayed schedule?

00:10:48.179 --> 00:10:48.980
Master Fu just now

00:10:48.980 --> 00:10:50.539
has already fully demonstrated.

00:10:50.539 --> 00:10:51.940
As long as we succeed once,

00:10:52.340 --> 00:10:53.299
catching up to the schedule

00:10:53.340 --> 00:10:54.220
won't be a problem.

00:10:54.419 --> 00:10:55.179
But who can guarantee

00:10:55.179 --> 00:10:56.340
the next attempt will succeed?

00:10:57.299 --> 00:10:57.980
What we're building

00:10:57.980 --> 00:10:59.059
is China's tallest building.

00:10:59.059 --> 00:11:00.340
It costs 140 million.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:01.659
The whole nation is watching.

00:11:01.659 --> 00:11:03.179
Precisely because the whole nation is watching,

00:11:03.580 --> 00:11:04.580
we, the construction iron army,

00:11:05.059 --> 00:11:06.299
should set the example first.

00:11:10.179 --> 00:11:10.860
It seems

00:11:11.340 --> 00:11:11.940
even within your own team,

00:11:11.940 --> 00:11:13.460
you haven't reached a consensus.

00:11:18.539 --> 00:11:19.460
I'm the workers' representative.

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:20.700
Let me say a couple of things.

00:11:21.940 --> 00:11:23.779
If we switch back to traditional jump forming,

00:11:24.299 --> 00:11:25.220
we can still do it.

00:11:25.860 --> 00:11:26.820
But to be honest,

00:11:27.820 --> 00:11:28.460
it's demoralizing.

00:11:28.539 --> 00:11:29.059
All of us

00:11:29.059 --> 00:11:30.340
came here specifically for the new technology.

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:30.980
Yes.

00:11:31.179 --> 00:11:33.059
Since the higher-ups also support it,

00:11:34.860 --> 00:11:36.659
we workers are willing to gamble one more time.

00:11:36.940 --> 00:11:38.860
Once we succeed, we all gain honor.

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:40.299
Right, right.

00:11:43.460 --> 00:11:44.460
You can gamble,

00:11:44.659 --> 00:11:45.940
but who takes responsibility if you lose?

00:11:46.179 --> 00:11:47.700
The city leaders do support it,

00:11:48.059 --> 00:11:48.820
but do you know

00:11:48.820 --> 00:11:50.179
how much pressure they're under?

00:11:55.779 --> 00:11:57.100
Since our Third Bureau is here,

00:11:57.179 --> 00:11:57.940
this battle

00:11:58.179 --> 00:11:58.940
must be fought

00:11:58.940 --> 00:11:59.940
beautifully.

00:12:00.419 --> 00:12:01.940
I will apply to our superiors

00:12:01.940 --> 00:12:03.059
for a third experiment.

00:12:03.580 --> 00:12:05.580
Good, good, good.

00:12:09.620 --> 00:12:10.860
Darn it! Darn it!

00:12:11.100 --> 00:12:12.379
Latest from the weather bureau:

00:12:12.379 --> 00:12:13.620
a typhoon is about to hit.

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:14.899
Maximum wind force, level twelve.

00:12:19.059 --> 00:12:20.700
Attention all personnel!

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.580
The typhoon is moving

00:12:22.580 --> 00:12:24.820
west-northwest.

00:12:25.299 --> 00:12:27.299
Everyone must pay attention to safety!

00:12:27.299 --> 00:12:28.100
Rebar team!

00:12:28.299 --> 00:12:29.659
Move faster, everyone!

00:12:29.659 --> 00:12:30.259
Got it, got it!

00:12:30.259 --> 00:12:31.700
If the motors get soaked, they're ruined!

00:12:32.139 --> 00:12:32.860
Alright, alright!

00:12:33.899 --> 00:12:35.700
Protect the underground cables!

00:12:37.940 --> 00:12:38.779
Be careful!

00:12:38.779 --> 00:12:39.179
Okay!

00:12:39.659 --> 00:12:40.779
Give me a hand over here!

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:43.379
All personnel, watch your safety!

00:12:44.899 --> 00:12:45.539
Give it to me!

00:12:46.419 --> 00:12:47.779
Hurry up! Get a move on!

00:12:51.220 --> 00:12:52.580
Why is there water pooling over there?

00:12:52.820 --> 00:12:54.539
Is this water pump broken?

00:12:54.820 --> 00:12:55.580
Where's Old Zhang?

00:12:56.139 --> 00:12:56.860
Old Zhang!

00:12:56.860 --> 00:12:57.779
There's water here!

00:12:57.779 --> 00:12:59.539
Everyone, be careful!

00:12:59.899 --> 00:13:00.700
The lights! The lights!

00:13:01.059 --> 00:13:02.059
Don't panic, everyone!

00:13:02.940 --> 00:13:04.179
Hold on, everyone!

00:13:04.820 --> 00:13:05.620
Hold on!

00:13:06.379 --> 00:13:07.940
Quick, quick! Hold on! Hold on!

00:13:09.340 --> 00:13:10.059
The tower crane!

00:13:10.700 --> 00:13:12.100
The tower crane is going to fall!

00:13:19.220 --> 00:13:20.620
We need to release the limit switch!

00:13:21.220 --> 00:13:22.379
Where's the tower crane operator?

00:13:22.419 --> 00:13:23.460
Tower crane operator!

00:13:23.620 --> 00:13:24.659
He took the day off today.

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:29.899
It's too dangerous if it falls!

00:13:34.980 --> 00:13:35.700
Let's go, Xiaohong.

00:13:36.220 --> 00:13:37.740
Evacuate! Evacuate!

00:13:38.019 --> 00:13:39.460
Get out, now! Move!

00:13:53.100 --> 00:13:53.940
Who is that?

00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:55.259
Looks like Brother Lu.

00:13:58.620 --> 00:13:59.580
He's got a death wish!

00:14:07.820 --> 00:14:08.340
Sister Su!

00:14:08.860 --> 00:14:10.179
Your man's something else!

00:14:11.379 --> 00:14:12.460
The tower crane is secure!

00:14:12.620 --> 00:14:14.179
We hold the line tonight!

00:14:14.460 --> 00:14:15.820
Protect the foundation pit!

00:14:16.860 --> 00:14:18.220
Hold the line!

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:21.580
Crane's stable, let's secure all the building materials.

00:14:21.580 --> 00:14:22.940
Okay, I understand.

00:14:28.860 --> 00:14:30.580
How long will this wind last?

00:14:30.980 --> 00:14:33.179
We'll hold as long as it blows.

00:14:47.940 --> 00:14:48.820
You just love showing off.

00:14:49.259 --> 00:14:50.220
You're the one with no regard for your life.

00:14:50.220 --> 00:14:51.860
Damn right, I'm your man.

00:14:51.860 --> 00:14:53.379
I think you two are six of one and half a dozen of the other.

00:14:59.059 --> 00:14:59.700
Sister Su!

00:14:59.980 --> 00:15:01.100
Our dormitory collapsed!

00:15:01.460 --> 00:15:01.980
My qin!

00:15:05.340 --> 00:15:06.700
My qin is still in there!

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:07.820
Don't panic, I'll look for it.

00:15:16.980 --> 00:15:17.500
It's not here.

00:15:18.139 --> 00:15:19.500
It couldn't have been blown away, could it?

00:15:21.860 --> 00:15:22.340
Found it!

00:16:06.820 --> 00:16:08.259
The foundation pit is safe.

00:16:11.299 --> 00:16:12.580
But the shacks are wrecked.

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:21.460
Not bad, Sister Su.

00:16:22.019 --> 00:16:23.940
Look, I didn't salvage a thing.

00:16:24.460 --> 00:16:26.139
And you managed to salvage this old thing.

00:16:51.700 --> 00:16:52.940
I don't want to play anymore.

00:16:52.940 --> 00:16:54.139
Why do I keep making mistakes?

00:16:57.299 --> 00:16:58.059
Don't get discouraged, sweetie.

00:16:58.820 --> 00:16:59.460
Xiaoxiao.

00:17:02.740 --> 00:17:03.580
Grandpa.

00:17:03.580 --> 00:17:04.819
It's not that I'm slacking off.

00:17:04.859 --> 00:17:06.220
It's just getting harder and harder.

00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:06.980
I'm afraid of making mistakes.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:08.700
The more I learn, the harder it gets.

00:17:10.140 --> 00:17:11.980
What if your teacher now...

00:17:11.980 --> 00:17:13.180
...had you practice every day...

00:17:13.180 --> 00:17:14.299
...the same simple tunes...

00:17:14.299 --> 00:17:15.180
...from when you first started learning?

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:16.579
Those easy pieces.

00:17:16.579 --> 00:17:17.579
Would you want that?

00:17:20.420 --> 00:17:20.980
Exactly.

00:17:21.900 --> 00:17:23.140
Things that are too easy...

00:17:23.299 --> 00:17:25.940
...aren't interesting to do, right?

00:17:26.059 --> 00:17:26.660
Right?

00:17:33.779 --> 00:17:35.059
This is really bizarre.

00:17:35.579 --> 00:17:36.819
We've slipped three times already.

00:17:37.220 --> 00:17:38.299
Why isn't it working yet?

00:17:39.019 --> 00:17:40.980
They say it's because it's hot this time, the temperature is high...

00:17:41.700 --> 00:17:43.500
...so the concrete's curing time changed again.

00:17:43.819 --> 00:17:45.579
It's a new method, you have to test it.

00:17:46.140 --> 00:17:47.259
Test it every single day?

00:17:47.980 --> 00:17:49.180
When will it ever end?

00:17:49.940 --> 00:17:51.500
Daring to try is better than not trying at all.

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:53.420
Then what do you call going in circles?

00:17:53.420 --> 00:17:54.180
What's that?

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:00.660
You imitate it pretty well.

00:18:00.900 --> 00:18:02.420
Still cracking jokes here?

00:18:02.900 --> 00:18:03.579
The construction site across the way...

00:18:03.579 --> 00:18:05.220
...is using us as a cautionary tale.

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:07.019
People have mouths.

00:18:07.019 --> 00:18:08.019
Let them talk if they want.

00:18:09.259 --> 00:18:10.779
They across the way dare to laugh at us?

00:18:11.019 --> 00:18:12.579
Serves them right, stuck doing brick-concrete forever.

00:18:12.779 --> 00:18:14.900
Well, at least they've built something.

00:18:15.180 --> 00:18:15.779
Yeah.

00:18:16.220 --> 00:18:17.380
And what about us?

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:18.299
Here every day, building and tearing down...

00:18:18.299 --> 00:18:19.059
...tearing down and building.

00:18:19.059 --> 00:18:20.140
Several sites over there...

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:21.019
...are already finished.

00:18:21.019 --> 00:18:22.460
How many floors have we even built?

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:23.259
Enough from you.

00:18:23.259 --> 00:18:24.779
They haven't shorted your pay, have they?

00:18:24.779 --> 00:18:25.980
At most, it's just wasted some time.

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:27.740
You were the enthusiastic one back then.

00:18:28.140 --> 00:18:29.220
And now you're still talking tough.

00:18:29.299 --> 00:18:30.500
If we'd used slip-form casting earlier...

00:18:30.500 --> 00:18:31.579
...we'd be topping out by now.

00:18:31.579 --> 00:18:32.420
If you want slip-form...

00:18:32.420 --> 00:18:33.380
...go do it across the way!

00:18:33.700 --> 00:18:34.740
Stop your whining here!

00:18:34.819 --> 00:18:35.819
What did you just say?

00:18:38.779 --> 00:18:39.619
Hey, hey... say less.